  {
    "id": "189e7366fcfa7c92",
    "title": "Checkout.com Supports Best Buy Marketplace With the Next Phase of Its Payments Infrastructure",
    "summary": "Checkout.com, a leading global digital payments company, today announced it will support Best Buy with the next phase of the retailer’s Marketplace payments infrastructure.\nBest Buy has evolved its strategy to meet more of customers’ technology needs by expanding its assortment with the launch of Best Buy Marketplace, which allows third-party sellers to seamlessly integrate their products into BestBuy.com and the Best Buy App.  \nAs Best Buy continues to advance its digital commerce business, the company is modernizing the payments infrastructure behind it. Teaming up with Checkout.com gives Best Buy a flexible foundation to extend its reach to a broader seller base.\nThrough this work, Checkout.com will provide card acquiring and debit routing capabilities, supported by flexible payments technology built to adapt as Best Buy’s needs evolve. This will support Best Buy Marketplace’s current payment flows while giving its team a foundation for future payment methods, geographies, and commerce models.\nCheckout.com will deliver dedicated enterprise support and industry expertise to help Best Buy navigate the complexities of various digital channels and settlement flows.\nAntoine Nougué, Chief Revenue Officer at Checkout.com, comments: “Best Buy has built a trusted experience to help customers navigate increasingly complex technology purchases. We’re proud to support the next phase of that evolution with modular technology, AI-powered payment optimization, and a hands-on approach to continued innovation and growth.”\nNoYesPayments09 Sep, 2026",
    "hasSummary": true,
    "link": "https://financialit.net/news/payments/checkoutcom-supports-best-buy-marketplace-next-phase-its-payments-infrastructure",
    "source": "Financial IT",
    "tags": [
      "Checkout.com",
      "Best Buy"
    ],
    "origin": "rss",
    "pubDate": "2026-09-09T07:49:07.000Z",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-09-09T09:01:19.686Z",
    "isDuplicateOf": null,
    "content": "Checkout.com has announced it is partnering with Best Buy to support the next phase of the retailer's Marketplace payments infrastructure. By teaming up with Checkout.com, Best Buy aims to modernize its digital commerce business, enabling flexible card acquiring and debit routing capabilities. The collaboration provides a foundation to help Best Buy adapt as its marketplace needs evolve and expand its reach to a broader seller base.",
    "slug": "checkout-com-supports-best-buy-marketplace-with-the-next-phase-of-its-payments-infrastructure"
  },
